course: dictionary
lesson: 11493
title: Big words for groups and totals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Aggregation means bringing many things together into one group or one total. The word is big, but the idea is simple: lots of separate things become one thing. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: «A huge aggregation of ladybirds covered the rose bush.» Many ladybirds gathered in one place make a group, so an aggregation is a group. Check it: swap in the word group, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «The teacher used aggregation to add all the spelling scores into one total.» Here the clues are scores and total. Maths and data use the same idea: many numbers combined into one. When the context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: Aggregation means bringing many things together into one group or total.
fact: An aggregation is a group or mass of things, animals or people gathered together.
fact: In data and maths, aggregation means combining many numbers into one, such as a total or an average.
fact: «News aggregation» means a website that collects news from many different sources in one place.
fact: Scientists use the word for groups of animals, such as «an aggregation of ladybirds» or «an aggregation of fish».
exercise: «A large aggregation of fish swam past the boat.» What is an aggregation here? | A fishing net | *A group of fish gathered together | A quiet lake | A single fish swimming alone
exercise: The class spelling marks were combined into one total. What does aggregation mean when used with data? | Counting the children one by one | Writing the numbers in order | Losing the scores | *Combining many numbers into one total
exercise: «The bees formed a huge aggregation around the hive.» Find and copy the word that names the group. | huge | *aggregation | hive | bees
test: Rachel says aggregation is a sort of mess with things thrown everywhere. Is she right? | Yes, it means a mess of things thrown around | *No, it means many things brought together into one group | Yes, it means a broken heap | No, it means one lonely thing
test: «News aggregation» collects stories from many newspapers. What does aggregation do here? | Writes one new story about cats | Hides all the news from readers | *Gathers many sources together in one place | Deletes old news
exam: In the sentence «A huge aggregation of starlings filled the sky», what does aggregation mean? | A type of weather | A quiet, empty sky | A single bird flying high | *A large group of birds gathered together
